{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"748","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Santa Clauses and a Soccer Championship"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The country Treeland consists of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" cities connected with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" bidirectional roads in such a way that it's possible to reach every city starting from any other city using these roads. There will be a soccer championship next year, and all participants are Santa Clauses. There are exactly "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2k"},{"kind":"text","text":" teams from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2k"},{"kind":"text","text":" different cities."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"During the first stage all teams are divided into "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" pairs. Teams of each pair play two games against each other: one in the hometown of the first team, and the other in the hometown of the other team. Thus, each of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2k"},{"kind":"text","text":" cities holds exactly one soccer game. However, it's not decided yet how to divide teams into pairs."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It's also necessary to choose several cities to settle players in. Organizers tend to use "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"as few cities as possible"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" to settle the teams."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Nobody wants to travel too much during the championship, so if a team plays in cities "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"u"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"text","text":", it wants to live in one of the cities on the shortest path between "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"u"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"text","text":" (maybe, in "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"u"},{"kind":"text","text":" or in "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"text","text":"). There is another constraint also: the teams from one pair must live in the same city."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Summarizing, the organizers want to divide "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2k"},{"kind":"text","text":" teams into pairs and settle them in the minimum possible number of cities "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" in such a way that teams from each pair live in the same city which lies between their hometowns."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 ≤ n ≤ 2·105, 2 ≤ 2k ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of cities in Treeland and the number of pairs of teams, respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The following "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines describe roads in Treeland: each of these lines contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ a, b ≤ n, a ≠ b"},{"kind":"text","text":") which mean that there is a road between cities "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":". It's guaranteed that there is a path between any two cities."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The last line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2k"},{"kind":"text","text":" distinct integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c1, c2, ..., c2k"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ci ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":"), where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ci"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the hometown of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th team. All these numbers are distinct."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of output must contain the only positive integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" which should be equal to the minimum possible number of cities the teams can be settled in."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line should contain "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" distinct numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"d1, d2, ..., dm"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ di ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":") denoting the indices of the cities where the teams should be settled."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines should follow, the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th of them should contain "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"uj"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"vj"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xj"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"uj"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"vj"},{"kind":"text","text":" are the hometowns of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th pair's teams, and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xj"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the city they should live in during the tournament. Each of the numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c1, c2, ..., c2k"},{"kind":"text","text":" should occur in all "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"uj"},{"kind":"text","text":"'s and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"vj"},{"kind":"text","text":"'s exactly once. Each of the numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xj"},{"kind":"text","text":" should belong to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"{d1, d2, ..., dm}"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are several possible answers, print any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6 2\n1 2\n1 3\n2 4\n2 5\n3 6\n2 5 4 6\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n2\n5 4 2\n6 2 2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test the orginizers can settle all the teams in the city number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":". The way to divide all teams into pairs is not important, since all requirements are satisfied anyway, because the city "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" lies on the shortest path between every two cities from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"{2, 4, 5, 6}"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"748F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/748/problem/F"}